e|fc_0ef79673c21a0eb20169ba66cb9d588191b232fe1ec2aa3cfd","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"sh -lc 'openclaw status || true; echo ---CONFIG-CANDIDATES---; find ~ -maxdepth 3 \\( -path \"*/openclaw*.json\" -o -path \"*/openclaw*.yaml\" -o -path \"*/openclaw*.yml\" -o -path \"*/config.json\" -o -path \"*/config.yaml\" -o -path \"*/config.yml\" \\) 2>/dev/null | grep -E \"openclaw|\\.openclaw|\\.config/openclaw\" | sed -n \"1,200p\"'","workdir":"/root/.openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000,"timeout":40},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"sh -lc 'openclaw status || true; echo ---CONFIG-CANDIDATES---; find ~ -maxdepth 3 \\\\( -path \\\"*/openclaw*.json\\\" -o -path \\\"*/openclaw*.yaml\\\" -o -path \\\"*/openclaw*.yml\\\" -o -path \\\"*/config.json\\\" -o -path \\\"*/config.yaml\\\" -o -path \\\"*/config.yml\\\" \\\\) 2>/dev/null | grep -E \\\"openclaw|\\\\.openclaw|\\\\.config/openclaw\\\" | sed -n \\\"1,200p\\\"'\",\"workdir\":\"/root/.openclaw/workspace\",\"yieldMs\":10000,\"timeout\":40}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":239,"output":602,"cacheRead":25472,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":26313,"cost":{"input":0.0005975,"output":0.00903,"cacheRead":0.0063679999999999995,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0159955}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773823673261}}
{"type":"message","id":"eadee900","parentId":"0de5bf08","timestamp":"2026-03-18T08:48:11.870Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_gXnElWszwZAj6lWslCvsHIEI|fc_0ef79673c21a0eb20169ba66cb9d44819191a763dc98f628e1","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"error\": \"missing_brave_api_key\",\n  \"message\": \"web_search (brave) needs a Brave Search API key. Run `openclaw configure --section web` to store it, or set BRAVE_API_KEY in the Gateway environment.\",\n  \"docs\": \"https://docs.openclaw.ai/tools/web\"\n}"}],"details":{"error":"missing_brave_api_key","message":"web_search (brave) needs a Brave Search API key. Run `openclaw configure --section web` to store it, or set BRAVE_API_KEY in the Gateway environment.","docs":"https://docs.openclaw.ai/tools/web"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1773823691844}}
{"type":"message","id":"bf657329","parentId":"eadee900","timestamp":"2026-03-18T08:48:12.138Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Jq6mJEcnHuwo1QATFXFJxlBd|fc_0ef79673c21a0eb20169ba66cb9d508191bc40ff83a9d6f0b9","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/security.md:26:The audit warns when multiple DM senders share the main session and recommends **secure DM mode**: `session.dmScope=\"per-channel-peer\"` (or `per-account-channel-peer` for multi-account channels) for shared inboxes.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/security.md:29:For intentional shared-user setups, the audit guidance is to sandbox all sessions, keep filesystem access workspace-scoped, and keep personal/private identities or credentials off that runtime.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/security.md:32:It also warns when sandbox Docker settings are configured while sandbox mode is off, when `gateway.nodes.denyCommands` uses ineffective pattern-like/unknown entries (exact node command-name matching only, not shell-text filtering), when `gateway.nodes.allowCommands` explicitly enables dangerous node commands, when global `tools.profile=\"minimal\"` is overridden by agent tool profiles, when open groups expose runtime/filesystem tools without sandbox/workspace guards, and when installed extension plugin tools may be reachable under permissive tool policy.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/security.md:62:- flips common `groupPolicy=\"open\"` to `groupPolicy=\"allowlist\"` (including account variants in supported channels)\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/index.md:315:Initialize config + workspace.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/index.md:319:- `--workspace <dir>`: agent workspace path (default `~/.openclaw/workspace`).\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/index.md:330:Interactive wizard to set up gateway, workspace, and skills.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/index.md:334:- `--workspace <dir>`\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/index.md:336:- `--reset-scope <config|config+creds+sessions|full>` (default `config+creds+sessions`; use `full` to also remove workspace)\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/index.md:406:- `--no-workspace-suggestions`: disable workspace memory hints.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/index.md:424:  - When adding a non-default account to a channel still using single-account top-level config, OpenClaw moves account-scoped values into `channels.<channel>.accounts.default` before writing the new account.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/index.md:425:  - Non-interactive `channels add` does not auto-create/upgrade bindings; channel-only bindings continue to match the default account.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/index.md:576:Manage isolated agents (workspaces + auth + routing).\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/index.md:585:- `--bindings`\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/index.md:589:Add a new isolated agent. Runs the guided wizard unless flags (or `--non-interactive`) are passed; `--workspace` is required in non-interactive mode.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/index.md:593:- `--workspace <dir>`\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/index.md:602:#### `agents bindings`\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/index.md:604:List routing bindings.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/index.md:613:Add routing bindings for an agent.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/index.md:623:Remove routing bindings for an agent.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/index.md:634:Delete an agent and prune its workspace + state.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/index.md:728:- `--workspace`\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/index.md:757:- `--reset` (reset dev config + credentials + sessions + workspace)\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/skills.md:11:Inspect skills (bundled + workspace + managed overrides) and see what’s eligible vs missing requirements.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/hooks.md:24:List all discovered hooks from workspace, managed, and bundled directories.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/hooks.md:39:  📎 bootstrap-extra-files ✓ - Inject extra workspace bootstrap files during agent bootstrap\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/hooks.md:97:  Config: ✓ workspace.dir\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/hooks.md:263:**Output:** `~/.openclaw/workspace/memory/YYYY-MM-DD-slug.md`\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/sandbox.md:20:Inspect the **effective** sandbox mode/scope/workspace access, sandbox tool policy, and elevated gates (with fix-it config key paths).\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/sandbox.md:151:- [Agent Configuration](/concepts/agent-workspace)\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/tui.md:20:- When launched from inside a configured agent workspace directory, TUI auto-selects that agent for the session key default (unless `--session` is explicitly `agent:<id>:...`).\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/tui.md:28:# when run inside an agent workspace, infers that agent automatically\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/channels.md:44:If you confirm bind now, the wizard asks which agent should own each configured channel account and writes account-scoped routing bindings.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/channels.md:46:You can also manage the same routing rules later with `openclaw agents bindings`, `openclaw agents bind`, and `openclaw agents unbind` (see [agents](/cli/agents)).\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/channels.md:48:When you add a non-default account to a channel that is still using single-account top-level settings (no `channels.<channel>.accounts` entries yet), OpenClaw moves account-scoped single-account top-level values into `channels.<channel>.accounts.default`, then writes the new account. This preserves the original account behavior while moving to the multi-account shape.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/channels.md:52:- Existing channel-only bindings (no `accountId`) continue to match the default account.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/channels.md:53:- `channels add` does not auto-create or rewrite bindings in non-interactive mode.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/channels.md:54:- Interactive setup can optionally add account-scoped bindings.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/channels.md:56:If your config was already in a mixed state (named accounts present, missing `default`, and top-level single-account values still set), run `openclaw doctor --fix` to move account-scoped values into `accounts.default`.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/gateway.md:54:- `--dev`: create a dev config + workspace if missing (skips BOOTSTRAP.md).\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/gateway.md:55:- `--reset`: reset dev config + credentials + sessions + workspace (requires `--dev`).\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/agents.md:2:summary: \"CLI reference for `openclaw agents` (list/add/delete/bindings/bind/unbind/set identity)\"\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/agents.md:4:  - You want multiple isolated agents (workspaces + routing + auth)\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/agents.md:10:Manage isolated agents (workspaces + auth + routing).\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/agents.md:15:- Agent workspace: [Agent workspace](/concepts/agent-workspace)\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/agents.md:21:openclaw agents add work --workspace ~/.openclaw/workspace-work\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/agents.md:22:openclaw agents bindings\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/agents.md:25:openclaw agents set-identity --workspace ~/.openclaw/workspace --from-identity\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/agents.md:30:## Routing bindings\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/agents.md:32:Use routing bindings to pin inbound channel traffic to a specific agent.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/agents.md:34:List bindings:\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/agents.md:37:openclaw agents bindings\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/agents.md:38:openclaw agents bindings --agent work\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/agents.md:39:openclaw agents bindings --json\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/agents.md:42:Add bindings:\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/agents.md:68:Remove bindings:\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/agents.md:77:Each agent workspace can include an `IDENTITY.md` at the workspace root:\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/agents.md:79:- Example path: `~/.openclaw/workspace/IDENTITY.md`\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/agents.md:80:- `set-identity --from-identity` reads from the workspace root (or an explicit `--identity-file`)\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/agents.md:82:Avatar paths resolve relative to the workspace root.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/agents.md:91:- `avatar` (workspace-relative path, http(s) URL, or data URI)\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/agents.md:96:openclaw agents set-identity --workspace ~/.openclaw/workspace --from-identity\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/onboard.md:4:  - You want guided setup for gateway, workspace, auth, channels, and skills\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/backup.md:11:Create a local backup archive for OpenClaw state, config, credentials, sessions, and optionally workspaces.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/backup.md:18:openclaw backup create --no-include-workspace\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/backup.md:29:- Output paths inside the source state/workspace trees are rejected to avoid self-inclusion.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/backup.md:41:- Workspace directories discovered from the current config, unless you pass `--no-include-workspace`\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/backup.md:43:If you use `--only-config`, OpenClaw skips state, credentials, and workspace discovery and archives only the active config file path.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/backup.md:45:OpenClaw canonicalizes paths before building the archive. If config, credentials, or a workspace already live inside the state directory, they are not duplicated as separate top-level backup sources. Missing paths are skipped.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/backup.md:51:`openclaw backup` intentionally bypasses the normal config preflight so it can still help during recovery. Because workspace discovery depends on a valid config, `openclaw backup create` now fails fast when the config file exists but is invalid and workspace backup is still enabled.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/backup.md:56:openclaw backup create --no-include-workspace\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/backup.md:59:That keeps state, config, and credentials in scope while skipping workspace discovery entirely.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/backup.md:61:If you only need a copy of the config file itself, `--only-config` also works when the config is malformed because it does not rely on parsing the config for workspace discovery.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/backup.md:70:- Time to walk large workspace trees and compress them into a `.tar.gz`\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/backup.md:74:Large workspaces are usually the main driver of archive size. If you want a smaller or faster backup, use `--no-include-workspace`.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/cron.md:71:`--light-context` applies to isolated agent-turn jobs only. For cron runs, lightweight mode keeps bootstrap context empty instead of injecting the full workspace bootstrap set.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/uninstall.md:20:Run `openclaw backup create` first if you want a restorable snapshot before removing state or workspaces.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/setup.md:2:summary: \"CLI reference for `openclaw setup` (initialize config + workspace)\"\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/setup.md:5:  - You want to set the default workspace path\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/setup.md:11:Initialize `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` and the agent workspace.\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/setup.md:22:openclaw setup --workspace ~/.openclaw/workspace\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/config.md:32:openclaw config get agents.defaults.workspace\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/cli/security.md:32:当多个私信发送者共享主会话时，审计会发出警告，并建议对共享收件箱使用 `session.dmScope=\"per-channel-peer\"`（或多账户渠道使用 `per-account-channel-peer`）。\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/cli/index.md:293:- `--workspace <dir>`：智能体工作区路径（默认 `~/.openclaw/workspace`）。\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/cli/index.md:308:- `--workspace <dir>`\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/cli/index.md:367:- `--no-workspace-suggestions`：禁用工作区记忆提示。\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6_hono@4.12.7_node-llama-cpp@3.16.2/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/cli/index.md:529:- `--bindings`\n/root/.local/share/pnpm/global/5/.pnpm/openclaw@2026.3.8_@napi-rs+canvas@0.1.96_@types+express@5.0.6