': '/root/.openclaw/workspaces/review', 'agentDir': '/root/.openclaw/agents/review/agent'}\n{'agentId': 'qa', 'accountId': 'qa', 'channel': 'feishu', 'binding_ok': 'qa', 'workspace': '/root/.openclaw/workspaces/qa', 'agentDir': '/root/.openclaw/agents/qa/agent'}","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1773824572087}}
{"type":"message","id":"1df04bfa","parentId":"80aab514","timestamp":"2026-03-18T09:03:01.253Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_3PlT3umG7GUqNow3tC4DOaR2|fc_0ef79673c21a0eb20169ba6a3bc6808191a32e8154d5a64ccc","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[plugins] plugins.allow is empty; discovered non-bundled plugins may auto-load: adp-openclaw (/root/.openclaw/extensions/adp-openclaw/index.ts), ddingtalk (/root/.openclaw/extensions/ddingtalk/index.ts), openclaw-plugin-yuanbao (/root/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-plugin-yuanbao/dist/index.js), openclaw-qqbot (/root/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-qqbot/index.ts), pinchtab (/root/.openclaw/extensions/pinchtab/index.ts), skillhub (/root/.openclaw/extensions/skillhub/index.ts) (+1 more). Set plugins.allow to explicit trusted ids.\n[plugins] skillhub: loaded without install/load-path provenance; treat as untracked local code and pin trust via plugins.allow or install records (/root/.openclaw/extensions/skillhub/index.ts)\n[plugins] feishu_doc: Registered feishu_doc, feishu_app_scopes\n[plugins] feishu_chat: Registered feishu_chat tool\n[plugins] feishu_wiki: Registered feishu_wiki tool\n[plugins] feishu_drive: Registered feishu_drive tool\n[plugins] feishu_bitable: Registered bitable tools\n[adp-openclaw] register() called - starting plugin registration\n[plugins] [adp-openclaw] Plugin register() called\n[adp-openclaw] Registering tool factory: adp_upload_file\n[plugins] [adp-openclaw] Registering tool factory: adp_upload_file\n[adp-openclaw] Tool adp_upload_file registered successfully\n[plugins] [adp-openclaw] Tool adp_upload_file registered successfully\n[adp-openclaw] Plugin registration complete\n[plugins] [adp-openclaw] Plugin registration complete\nOpenClaw security audit\nSummary: 9 critical · 9 warn · 1 info\nRun deeper: openclaw security audit --deep\n\nCRITICAL\ngateway.control_ui.host_header_origin_fallback DANGEROUS: Host-header origin fallback enabled\n  gateway.controlUi.dangerouslyAllowHostHeaderOriginFallback=true enables Host-header origin fallback for Control UI/WebChat websocket checks and weakens DNS rebinding protections.\n  Fix: Disable gateway.controlUi.dangerouslyAllowHostHeaderOriginFallback and configure explicit gateway.controlUi.allowedOrigins.\ngateway.control_ui.device_auth_disabled DANGEROUS: Control UI device auth disabled\n  gateway.controlUi.dangerouslyDisableDeviceAuth=true disables device identity checks for the Control UI.\n  Fix: Disable it unless you are in a short-lived break-glass scenario.\nsecurity.exposure.open_groups_with_elevated Open groupPolicy with elevated tools enabled\n  Found groupPolicy=\"open\" at:\n- channels.feishu.groupPolicy\nWith tools.elevated enabled, a prompt injection in those rooms can become a high-impact incident.\n  Fix: Set groupPolicy=\"allowlist\" and keep elevated allowlists extremely tight.\nsecurity.exposure.open_groups_with_runtime_or_fs Open groupPolicy with runtime/filesystem tools exposed\n  Found groupPolicy=\"open\" at:\n- channels.feishu.groupPolicy\nRisky tool exposure contexts:\n- agents.defaults (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.main (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.research (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.execution (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.review (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.qa (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\nPrompt injection in open groups can trigger command/file actions in these contexts.\n  Fix: For open groups, prefer tools.profile=\"messaging\" (or deny group:runtime/group:fs), set tools.fs.workspaceOnly=true, and use agents.defaults.sandbox.mode=\"all\" for exposed agents.\nchannels.feishu.warning.1 Feishu security warning\n  Feishu[default] groups: groupPolicy=\"open\" allows any member to trigger (mention-gated). Set channels.feishu.groupPolicy=\"allowlist\" + channels.feishu.groupAllowFrom to restrict senders.\nchannels.feishu.warning.2 Feishu security warning\n  Feishu[execution] groups: groupPolicy=\"open\" allows any member to trigger (mention-gated). Set channels.feishu.groupPolicy=\"allowlist\" + channels.feishu.groupAllowFrom to restrict senders.\nchannels.feishu.warning.3 Feishu security warning\n  Feishu[qa] groups: groupPolicy=\"open\" allows any member to trigger (mention-gated). Set channels.feishu.groupPolicy=\"allowlist\" + channels.feishu.groupAllowFrom to restrict senders.\nchannels.feishu.warning.4 Feishu security warning\n  Feishu[research] groups: groupPolicy=\"open\" allows any member to trigger (mention-gated). Set channels.feishu.groupPolicy=\"allowlist\" + channels.feishu.groupAllowFrom to restrict senders.\nchannels.feishu.warning.5 Feishu security warning\n  Feishu[review] groups: groupPolicy=\"open\" allows any member to trigger (mention-gated). Set channels.feishu.groupPolicy=\"allowlist\" + channels.feishu.groupAllowFrom to restrict senders.\n\nWARN\ngateway.control_ui.insecure_auth Control UI insecure auth toggle enabled\n  gateway.controlUi.allowInsecureAuth=true does not bypass secure context or device identity checks; only dangerouslyDisableDeviceAuth disables Control UI device identity checks.\n  Fix: Disable it or switch to HTTPS (Tailscale Serve) or localhost.\nchannels.feishu.doc_owner_open_id Feishu doc create can grant requester permissions\n  channels.feishu tools include \"doc\"; feishu_doc action \"create\" can grant document access to the trusted requesting Feishu user.\n  Fix: Disable channels.feishu.tools.doc when not needed, and restrict tool access for untrusted prompts.\nconfig.insecure_or_dangerous_flags Insecure or dangerous config flags enabled\n  Detected 3 enabled flag(s): gateway.controlUi.allowInsecureAuth=true, gateway.controlUi.dangerouslyAllowHostHeaderOriginFallback=true, gateway.controlUi.dangerouslyDisableDeviceAuth=true.\n  Fix: Disable these flags when not actively debugging, or keep deployment scoped to trusted/local-only networks.\ngateway.auth_no_rate_limit No auth rate limiting configured\n  gateway.bind is not loopback but no gateway.auth.rateLimit is configured. Without rate limiting, brute-force auth attacks are not mitigated.\n  Fix: Set gateway.auth.rateLimit (e.g. { maxAttempts: 10, windowMs: 60000, lockoutMs: 300000 }).\nsecurity.trust_model.multi_user_heuristic Potential multi-user setup detected (personal-assistant model warning)\n  Heuristic signals indicate this gateway may be reachable by multiple users:\n- channels.feishu.groupPolicy=\"open\"\nRuntime/process tools are exposed without full sandboxing in at least one context.\nPotential high-impact tool exposure contexts:\n- agents.defaults (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.main (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.research (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.execution (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.review (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.qa (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\nOpenClaw's default security model is personal-assistant (one trusted operator boundary), not hostile multi-tenant isolation on one shared gateway.\n  Fix: If users may be mutually untrusted, split trust boundaries (separate gateways + credentials, ideally separate OS users/hosts). If you intentionally run shared-user access, set agents.defaults.sandbox.mode=\"all\", keep tools.fs.workspaceOnly=true, deny runtime/fs/web tools unless required, and keep personal/private identities + credentials off that runtime.\nplugins.extensions_no_allowlist Extensions exist but plugins.allow is not set\n  Found 7 extension(s) under /root/.openclaw/extensions. Without plugins.allow, any discovered plugin id may load (depending on config and plugin behavior).\n  Fix: Set plugins.allow to an explicit list of plugin ids you trust.\nplugins.tools_reachable_permissive_policy Extension plugin tools may be reachable under permissive tool policy\n  Enabled extension plugins: adp-openclaw, ddingtalk, openclaw-plugin-yuanbao, openclaw-qqbot, pinchtab, skillhub, wecom.\nPermissive tool policy contexts:\n- default\n- agents.list.main\n- agents.list.research\n- agents.list.execution\n- agents.list.review\n- agents.list.qa\n  Fix: Use restrictive profiles (`minimal`/`coding`) or explicit tool allowlists that exclude plugin tools for agents handling untrusted input.\nplugins.installs_unpinned_npm_specs Plugin installs include unpinned npm specs\n  Unpinned plugin install records:\n- openclaw-qqbot (@tencent-connect/openclaw-qqbot)\n- ddingtalk (@largezhou/ddingtalk)\n- wecom (@mocrane/wecom)\n- adp-openclaw (adp-openclaw)\n  Fix: Pin install specs to exact versions (for example, `@scope/pkg@1.2.3`) for higher supply-chain stability.\nplugins.installs_missing_integrity Plugin installs are missing integrity metadata\n  Plugin install records missing integrity:\n- openclaw-qqbot\n- ddingtalk\n- wecom\n- adp-openclaw\n- openclaw-plugin-yuanbao\n  Fix: Reinstall or update plugins to refresh install metadata with resolved integrity hashes.\n\nINFO\nsummary.attack_surface Attack surface summary\n  groups: open=1, allowlist=0\ntools.elevated: enabled\nhooks.webhooks: disabled\nhooks.internal: disabled\nbrowser control: enabled\ntrust model: personal assistant (one trusted operator boundary), not hostile multi-tenant on one shared gateway"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":9156,"aggregated":"[plugins] plugins.allow is empty; discovered non-bundled plugins may auto-load: adp-openclaw (/root/.openclaw/extensions/adp-openclaw/index.ts), ddingtalk (/root/.openclaw/extensions/ddingtalk/index.ts), openclaw-plugin-yuanbao (/root/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-plugin-yuanbao/dist/index.js), openclaw-qqbot (/root/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-qqbot/index.ts), pinchtab (/root/.openclaw/extensions/pinchtab/index.ts), skillhub (/root/.openclaw/extensions/skillhub/index.ts) (+1 more). Set plugins.allow to explicit trusted ids.\n[plugins] skillhub: loaded without install/load-path provenance; treat as untracked local code and pin trust via plugins.allow or install records (/root/.openclaw/extensions/skillhub/index.ts)\n[plugins] feishu_doc: Registered feishu_doc, feishu_app_scopes\n[plugins] feishu_chat: Registered feishu_chat tool\n[plugins] feishu_wiki: Registered feishu_wiki tool\n[plugins] feishu_drive: Registered feishu_drive tool\n[plugins] feishu_bitable: Registered bitable tools\n[adp-openclaw] register() called - starting plugin registration\n[plugins] [adp-openclaw] Plugin register() called\n[adp-openclaw] Registering tool factory: adp_upload_file\n[plugins] [adp-openclaw] Registering tool factory: adp_upload_file\n[adp-openclaw] Tool adp_upload_file registered successfully\n[plugins] [adp-openclaw] Tool adp_upload_file registered successfully\n[adp-openclaw] Plugin registration complete\n[plugins] [adp-openclaw] Plugin registration complete\nOpenClaw security audit\nSummary: 9 critical · 9 warn · 1 info\nRun deeper: openclaw security audit --deep\n\nCRITICAL\ngateway.control_ui.host_header_origin_fallback DANGEROUS: Host-header origin fallback enabled\n  gateway.controlUi.dangerouslyAllowHostHeaderOriginFallback=true enables Host-header origin fallback for Control UI/WebChat websocket checks and weakens DNS rebinding protections.\n  Fix: Disable gateway.controlUi.dangerouslyAllowHostHeaderOriginFallback and configure explicit gateway.controlUi.allowedOrigins.\ngateway.control_ui.device_auth_disabled DANGEROUS: Control UI device auth disabled\n  gateway.controlUi.dangerouslyDisableDeviceAuth=true disables device identity checks for the Control UI.\n  Fix: Disable it unless you are in a short-lived break-glass scenario.\nsecurity.exposure.open_groups_with_elevated Open groupPolicy with elevated tools enabled\n  Found groupPolicy=\"open\" at:\n- channels.feishu.groupPolicy\nWith tools.elevated enabled, a prompt injection in those rooms can become a high-impact incident.\n  Fix: Set groupPolicy=\"allowlist\" and keep elevated allowlists extremely tight.\nsecurity.exposure.open_groups_with_runtime_or_fs Open groupPolicy with runtime/filesystem tools exposed\n  Found groupPolicy=\"open\" at:\n- channels.feishu.groupPolicy\nRisky tool exposure contexts:\n- agents.defaults (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.main (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.research (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.execution (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.review (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.qa (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\nPrompt injection in open groups can trigger command/file actions in these contexts.\n  Fix: For open groups, prefer tools.profile=\"messaging\" (or deny group:runtime/group:fs), set tools.fs.workspaceOnly=true, and use agents.defaults.sandbox.mode=\"all\" for exposed agents.\nchannels.feishu.warning.1 Feishu security warning\n  Feishu[default] groups: groupPolicy=\"open\" allows any member to trigger (mention-gated). Set channels.feishu.groupPolicy=\"allowlist\" + channels.feishu.groupAllowFrom to restrict senders.\nchannels.feishu.warning.2 Feishu security warning\n  Feishu[execution] groups: groupPolicy=\"open\" allows any member to trigger (mention-gated). Set channels.feishu.groupPolicy=\"allowlist\" + channels.feishu.groupAllowFrom to restrict senders.\nchannels.feishu.warning.3 Feishu security warning\n  Feishu[qa] groups: groupPolicy=\"open\" allows any member to trigger (mention-gated). Set channels.feishu.groupPolicy=\"allowlist\" + channels.feishu.groupAllowFrom to restrict senders.\nchannels.feishu.warning.4 Feishu security warning\n  Feishu[research] groups: groupPolicy=\"open\" allows any member to trigger (mention-gated). Set channels.feishu.groupPolicy=\"allowlist\" + channels.feishu.groupAllowFrom to restrict senders.\nchannels.feishu.warning.5 Feishu security warning\n  Feishu[review] groups: groupPolicy=\"open\" allows any member to trigger (mention-gated). Set channels.feishu.groupPolicy=\"allowlist\" + channels.feishu.groupAllowFrom to restrict senders.\n\nWARN\ngateway.control_ui.insecure_auth Control UI insecure auth toggle enabled\n  gateway.controlUi.allowInsecureAuth=true does not bypass secure context or device identity checks; only dangerouslyDisableDeviceAuth disables Control UI device identity checks.\n  Fix: Disable it or switch to HTTPS (Tailscale Serve) or localhost.\nchannels.feishu.doc_owner_open_id Feishu doc create can grant requester permissions\n  channels.feishu tools include \"doc\"; feishu_doc action \"create\" can grant document access to the trusted requesting Feishu user.\n  Fix: Disable channels.feishu.tools.doc when not needed, and restrict tool access for untrusted prompts.\nconfig.insecure_or_dangerous_flags Insecure or dangerous config flags enabled\n  Detected 3 enabled flag(s): gateway.controlUi.allowInsecureAuth=true, gateway.controlUi.dangerouslyAllowHostHeaderOriginFallback=true, gateway.controlUi.dangerouslyDisableDeviceAuth=true.\n  Fix: Disable these flags when not actively debugging, or keep deployment scoped to trusted/local-only networks.\ngateway.auth_no_rate_limit No auth rate limiting configured\n  gateway.bind is not loopback but no gateway.auth.rateLimit is configured. Without rate limiting, brute-force auth attacks are not mitigated.\n  Fix: Set gateway.auth.rateLimit (e.g. { maxAttempts: 10, windowMs: 60000, lockoutMs: 300000 }).\nsecurity.trust_model.multi_user_heuristic Potential multi-user setup detected (personal-assistant model warning)\n  Heuristic signals indicate this gateway may be reachable by multiple users:\n- channels.feishu.groupPolicy=\"open\"\nRuntime/process tools are exposed without full sandboxing in at least one context.\nPotential high-impact tool exposure contexts:\n- agents.defaults (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.main (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.research (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.execution (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.review (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.qa (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\nOpenClaw's default security model is personal-assistant (one trusted operator boundary), not hostile multi-tenant isolation on one shared gateway.\n  Fix: If users may be mutually untrusted, split trust boundaries (separate gateways + credentials, ideally separate OS users/hosts). If you intentionally run shared-user access, set agents.defaults.sandbox.mode=\"all\", keep tools.fs.workspaceOnly=true, deny runtime/fs/web tools unless required, and keep personal/private identities + credentials off that runtime.\nplugins.extensions_no_allowlist Extensions exist but plugins.allow is not set\n  Found 7 extension(s) under /root/.openclaw/extensions. Without plugins.allow, any discovered plugin id may load (depending on config and plugin behavior).\n  Fix: Set plugins.allow to an explicit list of plugin ids you trust.\nplugins.tools_reachable_permissive_policy Extension plugin tools may be reachable under permissive tool policy\n  Enabled extension plugins: adp-openclaw, ddingtalk, openclaw-plugin-yuanbao, openclaw-qqbot, pinchtab, skillhub, wecom.\nPermissive tool policy contexts:\n- default\n- agents.list.main\n- agents.list.research\n- agents.list.execution\n- agents.list.review\n- agents.list.qa\n  Fix: Use restrictive profiles (`minimal`/`coding`) or explicit tool allowlists that exclude plugin tools for agents handling untrusted input.\nplugins.installs_unpinned_npm_specs Plugin installs include unpinned npm specs\n  Unpinned plugin install records:\n- openclaw-qqbot (@tencent-connect/openclaw-qqbot)\n- ddingtalk (@largezhou/ddingtalk)\n- wecom (@mocrane/wecom)\n- adp-openclaw (adp-openclaw)\n  Fix: Pin install specs to exact versions (for example, `@scope/pkg@1.2.3`) for higher supply-chain stability.\nplugins.installs_missing_integrity Plugin installs are missing integrity metadata\n  Plugin install records missing integrity:\n- openclaw-qqbot\n- ddingtalk\n- wecom\n- adp-openclaw\n- openclaw-plugin-yuanbao\n  Fix: Reinstall or update plugins to refresh install metadata with resolved integrity hashes.\n\nINFO\nsummary.attack_surface Attack surface summary\n  groups: open=1, allowlist=0\ntools.elevated: enabled\nhooks.webhooks: disabled\nhooks.internal: disabled\nbrowser control: enabled\ntrust model: personal assistant (one trusted operator boundary), not hostile multi-tenant on one shared gateway","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1773824581243}}
{"type":"message","id":"8f1c7afa","parentId":"1df04bfa","timestamp":"2026-03-18T09:03:42.143Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0ef79673c21a0eb20169ba6a4b1bec8191957cbf28dd7f7a68\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpumpNeX2Mfz-OzUbzqFhIzLwa-SFfNnB-e8yuvdA6p_GVSsZg6stacK8O0yIrCOd4__831Z7e690OhLE-Hiqpocx-IDw02-sIYrNMHLbo-mLf5H8RwPV1ZbCWwQShrzI3DQ-k_VNACcuKF6C3MwIjMTx80zdJLy-Zrx523xlhLYOmB8K4zhJSEAJKMeC0oUvgUl_XuFWGB_9j87ZOiEW6OOKv6Z9A5-QfbWNTJxBHZonpzVQve4NFrFk2PTuIDTJnSkvniJUpvry7cCKUM3zfq9vg7I1R9XbPSRzM6nWDAlj6xFRHqfXkhrTmQSG4jklUX77ydg59pf_BbQthPbGozV5XIiojX6eJ4Psf0a4cl--7o3_x52snPAD5pC9edJZ4HvvmFLxlFVsp_vkIiQMY00gSouBhorzo70mRHSyuEwYSGqLP8U07cbog003ICdS9uEWVsf78n4N_r9Od6r0Q3Q0nLOBsaHVP8UlQ445rGV_8Ot6fbYZ8tBSzJdBs2r8c7IpvIo5y_FcU8USEBMzXm9x4hbcQswaw3_S1DJMeWSk1Y3hbljof8bosUKh8GU19M8zNjDvCtd9dm74KcP0vaptBW6FDuq54g0nqKR6KtixfkwQt4yV3y0Pg2aplqTLEvU0oRWs1G1FnAsohH22opphCIG-8UxkgnDl7fXSywPikPuEH48Qm4C0Z-J2pJSBGCAKkShkzXpQvjH4nW3q8vXXCx9_opnDXTBYFBvzoMI5zTI0QrpSAMAsxlF94yza-iDzU8sls9Wucp3AFa8x1XgVnSI1JtAVnminV5SMf_mtHDfP2la6ZxHGe4UYGxC9Whum1bb6dxi29ANw5BnqNByvpo2Erf5SRyPmAEGFDfxmN1Ph6u-UaeKkANP_TvkW-ZpUsDqdJkZZaDfN8fjwXZ6fAJKTGJe-SvY0Cp2eOmV-t2YwFCmZfwiKoh9iHOGihaoOsN_CP6CqjMjs-a6qgBqqESay_rkeXA1PmPPjcOdw-gBkhmoKQqa4GxYltAwImrwzRq1vbb1RDJzOlq4MSJVz-zksH3jcoen4KvJHh9ZJJeT8=\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] 继续验收结果如下。\n\n## A. 最终团队编制\n\n### 1) 主机器人\n- **botName**: 主机器人\n- **accountId**: `default`\n- **agentId**: `main`\n- **workspace**: `/root/.openclaw/workspace`\n- **agentDir**: `/root/.openclaw/agents/main/agent`\n- **role**: 总控 / 调度 / 兜底\n- **status**: **OK**\n\n### 2) 员工机器人：调研\n- **botName**: 调研机器人\n- **accountId**: `research`\n- **agentId**: `research`\n- **workspace**: `/root/.openclaw/workspaces/research`\n- **agentDir**: `/root/.openclaw/agents/research/agent`\n- **role**: 调研\n- **status**: **OK**\n\n### 3) 员工机器人：执行\n- **botName**: 执行机器人\n- **accountId**: `execution`\n- **agentId**: `execution`\n- **workspace**: `/root/.openclaw/workspaces/execution`\n- **agentDir**: `/root/.openclaw/agents/execution/agent`\n- **role**: 执行\n- **status**: **OK**\n\n### 4) 员工机器人：复核\n- **botName**: 复核机器人\n- **accountId**: `review`\n- **agentId**: `review`\n- **workspace**: `/root/.openclaw/workspaces/review`\n- **agentDir**: `/root/.openclaw/agents/review/agent`\n- **role**: 复核\n- **status**: **OK**\n\n### 5) 员工机器人：质检\n- **botName**: 质检机器人\n- **accountId**: `qa`\n- **agentId**: `qa`\n- **workspace**: `/root/.openclaw/workspaces/qa`\n- **agentDir**: `/root/.openclaw/agents/qa/agent`\n- **role**: 质检\n- **status**: **OK**\n\n---\n\n## B. 我修复了哪些问题\n\n### 已确认并修复\n1. **配置文件权限过宽**\n   - 已把 `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` 从世界可读修成 **600**\n\n### 已确认无问题\n2. **主机器人已纳入 `accounts.default`**\n   - 当前是：\n   - `channels.feishu.accounts.default = 主机器人`\n   - 不是残留在旧顶层单账号字段里\n\n3. **Feishu 已是纯 `accounts` 多账号结构**\n   - 已检查：\n   - **不存在**旧顶层单账号残留字段\n   - `legacy_top_level_fields = []`\n\n4. **DM 隔离已启用**\n   - `session.dmScope = per-account-channel-peer`\n\n5. **群内 @ 触发已启用**\n   - `channels.feishu.requireMention = true`\n\n6. **主机器人与员工机器人路由已一一对应**\n   - `default -> main`\n   - `research -> research`\n   - `execution -> execution`\n   - `review -> review`\n   - `qa -> qa`\n\n7. **每个机器人独立性已满足**\n   - 独立 `accountId`\n   - 独立 `agentId`\n   - 独立 `workspace`\n   - 独立 `agentDir`\n\n---\n\n## C. 当前生效策略\n\n- **多账户、多 Agent 完全隔离**\n- **DM 隔离**：`per-account-channel-peer`\n- **群策略**：`open`\n- **必须 @ 才响应**：`true`\n- **Feishu 出站默认账号**：`default`\n- **Feishu 连接模式**：`websocket`\n\n补一句关键说明：\n\n- 你现在这套是 **协作优先**\n- **不是安全优先**\n- 这和你的要求一致\n\n---\n\n## D. 已知风险\n\n这里我明确说清楚，不绕：\n\n1. **当前 `groupPolicy = open`**\n   - 意味着群里成员只要满足触发条件，就有机会唤起机器人\n   - 现在因为 `requireMention = true`，所以门槛是：**必须 @**\n\n2. **但 open + 强能力工具 = 安全审计一定会报警**\n   - 审计已经明确报了：\n   - open group\n   - runtime / filesystem tools 暴露\n   - elevated tools 启用\n\n3. **这不是搭建失败**\n   - 这是**策略选择导致的预期告警**\n   - 也就是：\n   - **系统是通的**\n   - **路由是对的**\n   - **机器人是在线的**\n   - **只是安全姿态偏开放**\n\n4. **还没做成“真实消息闭环验收”**\n   - 我已经做完了**配置级验证**和**运行状态验证**\n   - 但“群里必须 @ 才响应”“多账号私聊绝不串会话”这两项，要做到**最终 100% 闭环**，还需要你实际向不同机器人各发一条测试消息\n   - 原因很简单：这属于**真实入站事件验证**，不是只看配置就能证明到 100%\n\n---\n\n## E. 下一步建议\n\n只给最实用的 3 条：\n\n1. **立刻做 5 条真实消息验收**\n   - 给主机器人发 1 条私聊\n   - 给 4 个员工机器人分别发 1 条私聊\n   - 验证是否各自落到对应 agent、是否不串会话\n\n2. **拉一个测试群做 @ 验收**\n   - 先发**不 @** 的消息，看是否静默\n   - 再发 **@指定机器人** 的消息，看是否只由被 @ 的机器人响应\n\n3. **如果后面要上生产协作群**\n   - 把 `groupPolicy` 从 `open` 改成 `allowlist`\n   - 这是最直接的降风险动作\n   - 否则安全审计会持续报高风险，这不是 bug，是配置选择\n\n---\n\n## 本次验收结论\n\n**这台机器上的 Feishu 多机器人团队，配置层面已经通过。**\n当前状态是：\n\n- **结构正确**\n- **主机器人已规范进入 `accounts.default`**\n- **多账号隔离正确**\n- **路由正确**\n- **Feishu 通道正常**\n- **5/5 账号在线**\n- **唯一没做完的是“真实消息闭环测试”**\n\n如果你要，我下一步直接给你一份：\n\n**《5 分钟真实验收操作单》**\n\n你照着在飞书里发几条消息，我这边再根据返回结果给你做**最终 100% 验收结论**。","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0ef79673c21a0eb20169ba6a4db570819196d433bb8ec2d882\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":64484,"output":1568,"cacheRead":1536,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":67588,"cost":{"input":0.16121000000000002,"output":0.02352,"cacheRead":0.000384,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.185114}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773824581248}}
{"type":"message","id":"fb426288","parentId":"8f1c7afa","timestamp":"2026-03-18T12:02:19.851Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Skills store policy (operator configured):\n1. For skills discovery/install/update, try `skillhub` first (cn-optimized).\n2. If unavailable, rate-limited, or no match, fallback to `clawhub` (public-registry).\n3. Do not claim exclusivity. Public and private registries are both allowed.\n4. Before installation, summarize source, version, and notable risk signals.\n5. For search requests, execute `exec` with `skillhub search <keywords>` first and report the command output.\n6. In the current session, reply directly. Do NOT call `message` tool just to send progress updates.\n\nConversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b549d0a6770acb20bacc9965c34c\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\n  \"sender\": \"范\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Wed 2026-03-18 20:02 GMT+8\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"范 (ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8)\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\n  \"name\": \"范\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b549d0a6770acb20bacc9965c34c]\n范: 你说的 openclaw/openclaw.json 从世界可读修成 600 是什么意思"}],"timestamp":1773835339844}}
{"type":"message","id":"1eafca73","parentId":"fb426288","timestamp":"2026-03-18T12:02:37.776Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] 意思很简单：\n\n我把这个配置文件的 **Linux 文件权限** 改严了。\n\n### 原来\n`644`\n\n表示：\n- **文件主人** 可读可写\n- **同机其他用户** 可读\n- **其他所有用户** 也可读\n\n也就是：**这台机器上只要有别的账号，就能看这个文件内容。**\n\n### 现在\n`600`\n\n表示：\n- **只有文件主人** 可读可写\n- **其他任何用户** 都不能读、不能写\n\n### 为什么要改\n`~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` 里通常会放：\n- channel 配置\n- appId\n- appSecret\n- token\n- 路由和安全配置\n\n如果是 `644`，就属于**过宽权限**。\n虽然不代表已经泄露，但它确实是个安全风险。\n\n### 你可以这样理解\n- `644` = **门没锁，家里人能进，路过的人也能看**\n- `600` = **只有房主能开**\n\n### 我执行的命令\n```bash\nchmod 600 ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json\n```\n\n### 怎么验证\n```bash\nstat -c '%a %n' ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json\n```\n\n看到：\n```bash\n600 /root/.openclaw/openclaw.json\n```\n\n就说明已经生效。\n\n### 结论\n这次修改**不影响 OpenClaw 运行逻辑**，只是在**不改业务配置的前提下，把配置文件访问权限收紧**。\n\n如果你要，我也可以顺手把：\n- 哪些权限是 **Linux 常见安全基线**\n- `600 / 644 / 755 / 700` 分别该用在什么文件上\n\n给你整理成一张超短速查表。","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0ef79673c21a0eb20169ba945215a48191b6564d0419fb515a\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":66160,"output":414,"cacheRead":1536,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":68110,"cost":{"input":0.16540000000000002,"output":0.00621,"cacheRead":0.000384,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.171994}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773835339847}}
{"type":"message","id":"8cafb15a","parentId":"1eafca73","timestamp":"2026-03-18T12:07:21.438Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Skills store policy (operator configured):\n1. For skills discovery/install/update, try `skillhub` first (cn-optimized).\n2. If unavailable, rate-limited, or no match, fallback to `clawhub` (public-registry).\n3. Do not claim exclusivity. Public and private registries are both allowed.\n4. Before installation, summarize source, version, and notable risk signals.\n5. For search requests, execute `exec` with `skillhub search <keywords>` first and report the command output.\n6. In the current session, reply directly. Do NOT call `message` tool just to send progress updates.\n\nConversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b549d1946f8a0b10a90f34fa25fe\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\n  \"sender\": \"范\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Wed 2026-03-18 20:07 GMT+8\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"范 (ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8)\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\n  \"name\": \"范\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b549d1946f8a0b10a90f34fa25fe]\n范: 文件主人 可读可写 是指主机器人可读可写，其它机器人不可读写吗"}],"timestamp":1773835641431}}
